      "F7": "The high LDL-C level off lipid-lowering agents is more typical of primary hyperlipidaemias such as Familial Hypercholesterolemia and Familial Combined Hyperlipidemia.",
      "F8": "The direct LDL-C level of 113 mg/dL after treatment is more consistent with a diagnosis of Familial Hypercholesterolemia or Familial Combined Hyperlipidemia, which often respond to lipid-lowering therapy."
